{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"agent_message","text":"Folding the scale into projection weights was slower and reduced the narrowest correctness margin, so it has been reverted. I found a safer memory optimization instead: both Q scaling and softmax can reuse dead intermediates in place, producing bitwise-identical softmax values while avoiding large temporary allocations."}}
